# What this project is responsible for, and what happens when it breaks.
level: 1
owner: Eli Ferres
monitor: GitHub Actions on every push and pull request; the badge in the README is the health signal. Failures surface as issues.
rollback: git revert, then re-tag. Installed copies are pinned to a version and are unaffected until the user upgrades.
migrations: n/a: the tool owns no database and no schema. It reads other people's databases through their public REST door with the public key and changes nothing in them.
backups: n/a: the tool writes only its dated reports into the reports folder of the directory it runs in, which the user owns and versions as they see fit. A second run adds a file and overwrites nothing.
authz: n/a: no server and no trust boundary. It runs locally, as whoever invoked it, with exactly their permissions, and sends only GET and HEAD requests.
logs: n/a: a command-line tool that prints its findings and exits. The dated report is the record, and the caller decides where it goes.
alerts: n/a: nothing runs unattended. The tool is invoked by a person or a build, and a non-zero exit is how it raises its hand.
